    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200:\n- tree-sitter-groovy 0.1.2 does not parse an untyped parameter (`def f(x)`), the commonest form in Jenkins and Gradle code; `f(a, b)` still hashes a parameter name.\n- A default value is not hashed although each default generates an overload (owner's call; MOVES IDS).\n- Type parameters are hashed by name; record methods are emitted bare; traits do not parse.\n- Constructors, fields and properties are not Groovy symbols.\n\nFixing a part marked MOVES IDS changes hashed input, so it belongs to the next stable-id bump, with a measured churn figure in the spec's history row.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # 4194
